00,12.34],[1638316800,10.71],[1640995200,9.5],[1643673600,10.24],[1646092800,11.26],[1648771200,11.39],[1651363200,10.27],[1654041600,9.35],[1656633600,8.24],[1659312000,7.51],[1661990400,6.12],[1664582400,4.42],[1667260800,3.44],[1669852800,3.37],[1672531200,3.06],[1675209600,1.94],[1677628800,-0.7],[1680307200,-2.28],[1682899200,-3.03],[1685577600,-2.78],[1688169600,-2.58],[1690848000,-2.3],[1693526400,-1.27],[1696118400,-1.06],[1698796800,-0.78],[1701388800,-0.78],[1704067200,-1.2],[1706745600,-1.27],[1709251200,-0.85],[1711929600,-0.61],[1714521600,0],[1717200000,0.92],[1719792000,1.02],[1722470400,0.31],[1725148800,0.31],[1727740800,0.81],[1730419200,1.02],[1733011200,1.02],[1735689600,1.54],[1738368000,2.26],[1740787200,2.25],[1743465600,1.83],[1746057600,1.42],[1748736000,1.21],[1751328000,1.32],[1754006400,2.03],[1756684800,1.83],[1759276800,1.41],[1761955200,1.41],[1764547200,2.22],[1767225600,2.82],[1769904000,3.61],[1772323200,4.8],[1775001600,6.68],[1777593600,7.68],[1780272000,7.78],[1782864000,8.29],[1785542400,8.37],[1788220800,9.76]]}]}],"qna":[{"question":"What does the Wholesale Price Index (WPI) Inflation - Manufacturing data represent?","answer":"The Wholesale Price Index (WPI) Inflation - Manufacturing data represents the change in prices of manufactured goods at the wholesale level.^It is an indicator that measures and tracks the price changes of goods before they reach the retail level, specifically focusing on the manufacturing sector.^The manufacturing index covers prices of a wide range of manufactured products across various industries (a total of 564 items) and has a weight of 64.23% in WPI."},{"question":"What is the significance of the Wholesale Price Index (WPI) Inflation - Manufacturing data?","answer":"It serves as a key indicator of inflation trends within the manufacturing sector, and provides insights into cost pressures faced by manufacturers, which can impact profit margins and pricing strategies.^It indicates what cost pressures businesses are facing (from commodity prices), hence becomes an input for the CPI inflation.^Wholesale inflation trends reflect the supply-demand dynamics in the manufacturing sector, as price changes can be influenced by shifts in supply chain, production costs, and market demand.^Trends in WPI Inflation can impact tax policies, government spending, especially in areas related to the manufacturing sector."},{"question":"How to interpret the Wholesale Price Index (WPI) Inflation - Manufacturing data?","answer":"An increasing trend in WPI Inflation - Manufacturing suggests rising costs of manufacturing goods, potentially leading to higher retail inflation rates in the near-term. A decreasing trend might indicate lower inflationary pressures or declining demand.^Analysing the WPI data across different categories of manufacturing goods can reveal which specific sectors are experiencing higher price increases and may need attention in terms of supply chain management or policy intervention.^The WPI Inflation - Manufacturing data can be correlated with other economic indicators such as the Consumer Price Index (CPI) inflation, GDP growth, agriculture and industrial growth to gain a broader understanding of the economic and inflationary environment."}],"related":[{"slug":"bank-credit-industry","title":"Bank Credit - Industry"},{"slug":"capacity-utilisation","title":"Capacity Utilisation"},{"slug":"cement-production","title":"Cement Production"},{"slug":"energy-requirements","title":"Energy Requirements"},{"slug":"exports-manufactured-goods","title":"Exports - Manufactured Goods"},{"slug":"hsbc-manufacturing-purchasing-managers-index-pmi","title":"HSBC Manufacturing PMI"},{"slug":"index-of-industrial-production-iip-consumer-durables","title":"Index of Industrial Production (IIP)- Consumer Durables"},{"slug":"index-of-industrial-production-iip-consumer-non-durables","title":"Index of Industrial Production (IIP)- Consumer Non-Durables"},{"slug":"index-of-industrial-production-iip-electricity","title":"Index of Industrial Production (IIP)- Electricity"},{"slug":"index-of-industrial-production-iip-manufacturing","title":"Index of Industrial Production (IIP)- Manufacturing"},{"slug":"index-of-industrial-production-iip-mining","title":"Index of Industrial Production (IIP)- Mining"},{"slug":"natural-gas-production","title":"Natural Gas Production"},{"slug":"petroleum-consumption","title":"Petroleum Consumption"},{"slug":"steel-production","title":"Steel Production"}],"title":"Wholesale Price Index (WPI) Inflation - Manufacturing","description":"Manufacturing WPI inflation stands at 9.76% for Sep 2026. This component carries the largest weight in the WPI basket.","headline":{"Absolute":"Manufacturing WPI inflation stands at 110.2 for Sep 2026. This component carries the largest weight in the WPI basket.","Y-o-Y":"Manufacturing WPI inflation stands at 9.76% for Sep 2026. This component carries the largest weight in the WPI basket."},"source":"CMIE Economic Outlook, 1 Finance Research","source_url":"https://economicoutlook.cmie.com/","date_modified":"2026-09-01","scraped_at":"2026-10-19T15:05:14+00:00"}